/* book exam traps: Using P proportional to cos(Δφ) instead of cos²(Δφ/2) gives wrong nulls and wrong power at quadrature. | Calling Vπ the voltage for maximum transmission or for a 2π phase shift. Vπ gives the first null, a π phase difference. | Forgetting the push-pull factor: each arm gets ±Δφ/2, while interference depends on the total difference Δφ. | Mixing extinction ratio with insertion loss. Extinction ratio compares on and off levels of one modulator; insertion loss compares output with input. | Assuming an external modulator has zero chirp in every drive scheme. Single-arm drive and electro-absorption modulators can still chirp. */
